# Laravel

## Mục tiêu

Laravel là một PHP framework mạnh mẽ cho việc xây dựng web applications với syntax elegant và developer experience tuyệt vời. Trong Cursor Enterprise Framework, Laravel đóng vai trò là một trong những lựa chọn chính cho backend development, đặc biệt cho các dự án cần rapid development, robust ORM, built-in authentication, và comprehensive ecosystem.

Mục tiêu của rule này là hướng dẫn developers trong việc sử dụng Laravel hiệu quả trong enterprise context, từ project architecture, database design, API development, đến testing và deployment.

## Nguyên tắc

**1. Follow MVC Architecture**

Models cho data và business logic. Views cho presentation. Controllers cho request handling. Keep concerns separated. Don't bloat any layer.

**2. Use Eloquent Effectively**

Define relationships clearly. Use eager loading to avoid N+1. Use scopes for reusable queries. Use accessors và mutators. Leverage polymorphic relationships when needed.

**3. Service Layer Pattern**

Extract business logic to services. Keep controllers thin. Services are reusable. Better testability. Clear dependency injection.

**4. Repository Pattern for Data Access**

Abstract data access. Use interfaces for testability. Repositories handle queries. Services use repositories. Easy to swap implementations.

**5. Form Request Validation**

Use Form Request classes. Define validation rules clearly. Reuse across controllers. Type-hint in controller methods. Custom validation rules when needed.

**6. API Resource Classes**

Transform models consistently. Use API Resources. Include relationships properly. Pagination handling. Sparse fieldsets for performance.

**7. Queue Jobs for Async Work**

Move heavy work to queues. Email sending. Image processing. External API calls. Keep requests fast. Proper job retry logic.

**8. Database Migrations**

Version control database. Each migration reversible. Small, focused changes. Don't modify committed migrations. Use seeder for test data.

**9. Event-Driven Architecture**

Use Laravel Events. Decouple components. Queue event listeners. Easy audit trail. Clean extensibility.

**10. Testing First**

Write tests before code. Use feature tests for workflows. Use unit tests for logic. Test at appropriate level. Continuous integration.

